<% title "Set up payments — #{@event.name}" %>

<h1 class="heading">Set up payments for <%= @event.name %></h1>

<%# Fuime: the guardian-facing Stripe onboarding form.
    Two things in this page are deliberate and should not be "tidied":

    1. The warning about a Stripe window below. Because Fuime is configured so
       that STRIPE carries negative-balance liability rather than Fuime, Stripe
       necessarily also collects the identity requirements — and that combination
       means the guardian hits a Stripe-owned authentication popup inside this
       otherwise-embedded form. It cannot be disabled: the flag that would
       (`disable_stripe_user_authentication`) requires Fuime to collect
       requirements itself, which would mean owning every chargeback. Warning the
       guardian turns an alarming surprise into an expected security step, and is
       the highest-leverage sentence in the whole flow.

    2. The fee disclosure. Fuime's platform fee is charged on this account, and a
       platform is expected to disclose its fees to a connected account before
       imposing them. Saying it here, in the consent moment, is both the honest
       and the defensible place. %>

<%# Two audiences read this consent moment, and they are legally different
    parties. A guardian is an individual backing the account with their own
    identity; a school administrator is a representative completing it for the
    institution, whose EIN — not the administrator's own finances — anchors the
    account (business_type "company", see ConnectOnboardingService). Telling a
    business-office employee "you will own this payment account" was both wrong
    and alarming, which the first prod render of this page demonstrated. %>
<%= render "application/callout", type: "info", title: "What to expect" do %>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mb-2">
    <li class="mb-1">
      Stripe — Fuime's payments partner — will ask you to confirm your identity in
      a secure Stripe window. That step is Stripe's, not Fuime's.
    </li>
    <% if @event.institutionally_sponsored? %>
      <li class="mb-1">
        You'll enter your school's legal details — name, EIN and address — and
        yourself as the contact completing the form. Stripe also asks for the
        contact's name, date of birth, address and last four digits of their
        Social Security number; that identifies you as the school's
        representative, not as the seller of record. <strong>Fuime never sees
        or stores any of it</strong> — it goes directly to Stripe.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-1">
        <strong>Your school is the institutional sponsor, not the owner of a Stripe or payment account.</strong>
        <%= fuime_legal_seller %> (Fuime) is the seller of record.
        An administrator must approve the payout destination. This venture's
        books show a payable to the school — never to any employee personally.
      </li>
    <% else %>
      <li class="mb-1">
        You'll be asked for your name, date of birth, address and the last four
        digits of your Social Security number. <strong>Fuime never sees or stores
        any of it</strong> — it goes directly to Stripe.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-1">
        You are the legal payee and clawback obligor. You must approve the payout destination
        before the first payout. Your young founder runs the venture day to day.
      </li>
    <% end %>
    <li class="mb-0">
      Fuime's platform fee is
      <strong><%= number_to_percentage(@event.revenue_fee * 100, precision: 1) %></strong>
      of what the venture collects, charged on this account. Stripe's own card
      processing fee applies separately and goes to Stripe.
    </li>
  </ul>
<% end %>

<p class="muted text-sm"><%= fuime_status_line %></p>

<%# The component mounts here. Stripe's Connect JS is loaded and driven by the
    Stimulus controller in app/javascript/controllers/stripe_connect_onboarding_controller.js;
    the client secret is fetched fresh on each render because Account Sessions
    are short-lived. %>
<div
  data-controller="stripe-connect-onboarding"
  data-stripe-connect-onboarding-publishable-key-value="<%= @publishable_key %>"
  data-stripe-connect-onboarding-client-secret-value="<%= @client_secret %>"
  data-stripe-connect-onboarding-return-url-value="<%= fuime_payment_setup_return_path(event_slug: @event.slug) %>"
  data-stripe-connect-onboarding-refresh-url-value="<%= fuime_payment_setup_refresh_path(event_slug: @event.slug) %>"
  class="mt-4">
  <div data-stripe-connect-onboarding-target="container"></div>

  <%# Shown until the component mounts, and left in place if it never does — a
      blank rectangle gives a parent no way to tell "still loading" from "broken". %>
  <p data-stripe-connect-onboarding-target="fallback" class="muted text-sm">
    Loading Stripe's secure setup form…
    If this doesn't appear, check that your browser isn't blocking scripts from
    Stripe, then <%= link_to "try again", new_fuime_payment_setup_path(event_slug: @event.slug), class: "underline" %>.
  </p>
</div>

<p class="muted text-sm mt-4">
  <%= link_to "← Back to payment status", fuime_payment_setup_path(event_slug: @event.slug) %>
</p>
